@layout('layouts/main')
@section('body')

  <main>
    <div>
      <h1 class="title">arkivo.art</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">
        archive of network-interactive and evolving crypto-art
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>disclaimer: this is an early alpha release and is under heavy construction</strong>
      </p>

      <p>
        Goals of this project
      <p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          To identify and catalogue all network-interactive and other evolving crypto-artworks.
        </li>

        <li>
          To take regular snapshots of evolving artworks, including any network / API calls performed by the artwork during a snapshot.
        </li>

        <li>
          To scan interactive (code-based) artworks for potential vulnerabilities or malicious code.
        </li>

        <li>
          To document artworks as to aid in future conservation and restoration efforts.
        </li>

        <li>
          To apply restoration techniques to artworks which may have ceased to function as intended by the artist.
        </li>

        </ul>

        <p>
          <strong>Update:</strong> The PhD thesis on which this work is based is now <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Daniel-Farinha-2/publication/391213179_ARKIVO_An_Information_System_for_the_Preservation_of_Networked_Crypto_Art/links/680e5152df0e3f544f4b9453/ARKIVO-An-Information-System-for-the-Preservation-of-Networked-Crypto-Art.pdf" target="_blank">available online</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
          Note: currently this project only catalogs OBJKTs minted on the HEN smart contract. The scope of the catalog will increase over time.
        <p>

    </div>
  </main>

